 "traditions": [],
 "notes": "All six planned kinds kept; old models folded into archetype versions (Rolleiflex, Rolleicord, Mamiya C, Lubitel, Nettar, Bessa III, Technika, Sinar F, Chamonix 45H-1). Old flat models Superb, Retina, Box-Tengor and old ranges Brownie, Nettar, Rolleiflex, Mamiya C, Chamonix H/F, Technika, Sinar F became archetypes or versions. Models handed over from shelf 01_00 are included: Bronica RF645 and Mamiya 6 / 7 / 7 II (rangefinder archetypes), Hasselblad XPan / XPan II (panoramic archetype). Planned rangefinder models 'from k17' were not supplied in the brief, so only Fujifilm GA645 and GF670 (named on the Fujifilm page) sit in m. Not added for lack of a retrieved page with details: Fuji GSW690 and G690 versions, Hasselblad SWC as its own archetype (kept as a V-system version), Kodak Cirkut (maker not on page), Deardorff, Toyo, Wista, Ebony, Shen Hao, Agfa Isolette, Mamiya Six, Minolta Autocord. Some years omitted where pages gave none (Makina 67/670, Sinar F/X, Technikardan). Brand facts from knowledge: Pentax, LOMO, Lomography, Kodak, Chamonix country, Seitz; founding years for Hasselblad, Mamiya, Rollei, Fujifilm, Yashica, KMZ also from knowledge. No traditions: industrial products."
}